# Docker build context exclusions (repo root).
# Keep package*.json — required for deterministic npm ci layers!

node_modules
**/node_modules
.git
.github
docs
*.md
apps/web/dist
apps/web/android
apps/api/uploads
coverage
**/coverage
*.log
monitoring
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local development/test databases. docker/api.Dockerfile copies
# apps/api/prisma, so without these lines the shipped runtime image carried 23
# SQLite files (dev.db, test.db, e2e.db and twenty audit-*.db, ~21 MB) holding
# bcrypt password hashes, refresh-token hashes, payments and audit trails — found
# by the 10k-concurrency audit (F-01). The runtime stage now copies named paths
# instead of the whole directory; this is the outer of the two guards.
*.db
*.db-journal
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# Untracked local working artefacts. .gitignore already hides them from git, and
# CI never has them (it builds from a fresh clone) — but a local `docker build`
# did drag ~130 MB into the context and, because docker/web.Dockerfile ends with
# `COPY . .`, into the web builder layer: four debug APKs (32 MB), the audit and
# evidence trees, QA screenshots and jscpd output (F-84).
*.apk
tmp_*.mjs
api-full-validation.sh
New folder/
.audit*/
.audit-archive/
.agent-evidence/
qa-*/
jscpd-report/
